    "stewardship",
    "metadata"
  ],
  "derivedFrom": {
    "surface": "Studio > Catalog > Dataset > General",
    "capturedOn": "2026-08-18",
    "productVersion": "next.dev.zeenea.app"
  },
  "slots": {
    "header": "Identity row (type tag, sharing tag, title, status tag, Actions button) over three metadata lines: technical name, a catalog/category/connection path with links, and a last-updated date.",
    "tabs": "Nine object facets, some carrying a count, one disabled when the source supplies nothing. Opposite them, two avatar stacks: curators and contacts, which are a summary of the People panel below.",
    "left": "Authored narrative: access-request policy select, glossary multi-select of removable chips, a description block with a rich-text switch and a use-source checkbox, and a relations section that is empty far more often than not.",
    "right": "Completion meter, then a second tab set. Properties is a long label-and-control form mixing selects, multi-selects, plain values, date inputs with a format caption, and unset properties that read 'No data has been registered.', ending in a read-only source-properties definition list.",
    "right-people": "Not drawn here. Two role sections (Curator, Contact), each with an add-person icon action and a two-column grid of avatar, name and a remove control.",
    "right-suggestions": "Not drawn here. A four-way segmented control (Accepted, Rejected, Pending, All) over suggestion cards: author avatar, name, relative time, status at the right, body text, a comment textarea, and a Reject/Accept footer pair.",
    "toast": "Not drawn here. A transient error toast appears bottom-centre on a slow response. It is real chrome on this page, and the DS tier has no toast component to carry it."
  },
  "renderNotes": [
    "Inside a VERTICAL frame, never set `sizing.horizontal:\"FILL\"`. `render-node.js` emits `flex:1` for it with no axis awareness, so in a column it distributes HEIGHT; width already fills because the renderer only sets `align-items` when `counterAxisAlignItems` is given, so the flex default of `stretch` applies. FILL is correct only for children of a HORIZONTAL frame, which is why the two body columns carry it and nothing below them does. Plugin #298.",
    "`fmTabs` reads `Tabs` (a comma-separated string or an array) and `Active`. It has no per-tab children and no count badge, so a count has to be written into the label text.",
    "`fmUser` always renders initials AND the name (plugin #299), so an overlapping avatar stack is not expressible: it draws as a row of name chips. Keep stacks to three.",
    "`fmEmptyState` takes no props and always renders the words 'No items' (plugin #299). Any empty state with real copy must be composed from `fmPlaceholder` plus a TEXT sibling, as the relations section does here.",
    "`fmTextArea` reads only the `Content=` variant and no text prop (plugin #299), so the suggestion comment box cannot carry its placeholder. That is why the Suggestions panel is described in `slots` rather than drawn.",
    "`fmProgressBar` reads the VARIANT (`Completion=`), not props, and collapses to zero width in a centred row unless hosted in a fixed-width frame.",
    "`fmDropdown` carries its own label and caption via `Label Text` / `Caption Text` when `Show label` is not false. `fmDateInput` does not: its caption ('YYYY/MM/DD') must be a sibling TEXT.",
    "Prop keys may carry Figma's `#nodeId` suffix or not; `normalizeProps` in `fm-html-map.js` strips it, so `Label` and `Label#1411:32` are equivalent. Plain names are used here."
  ],
